  "behavior": [
    "Each owner selects authenticated WSS after actual QUIC Initial datagrams hit owned loopback UDP blackholes. Preferred/selected/fallback state is observed through the public owner API.",
    "For each of consult/handoff/replacement, capture a current authorized snapshot, submit the original control intent, explicitly reconnect and recover the exact scoped record plus finite authoritative journal catch-up. The owner never resubmits a mutation. The separate fixture retains explicit original replay/refusal checks from G6-051.",
    "Each old physical closes and invokes its lifetime callback once. Three explicit reconnects produce epochs 2,3,4 with one fresh enrollment resolution per epoch.",
    "An invalid current bearer is refused during authentication at epoch 5. Restoring valid current enrollment and explicitly reconnecting at epoch 6 restores selected WSS control. This is invalid-credential proof, not credential-expiry proof.",
    "Private read-only SQL oracle requires one original operation row, unchanged record/expiry/precondition, zero external effects and retained active source routes. Canonical native/HTTP/browser common status projections agree.",
    "Consult stays accepted without media preparation and is then cancelled. Handoff and replacement fail their exact unready preflight checks. No successful live media transition is inferred.",
    "Original accepted Message/Session invite/accept IDs remain preserved. Session end is confirmed; owned browser/Node/server and physical routes/slots are joined/retired."
  ],
